# SurfaceFlinger asks init to start the boot animation from its own init
# (ctl.start), but init handles that request only after 'class_start main'
# of the nonencrypted trigger, which takes over 2 s, and bootanimation then
# needs about 4 s before its first frame. Starting it right after
# 'class_start core' (which starts SurfaceFlinger) overlaps both;
# bootanimation waits for SurfaceFlinger by itself, and the later
# ctl.start is a no-op for a running service.
on boot
    start bootanim
